2. Create a small Python 3.11+ harness using only the standard library plus `matplotlib==3.8.4`. Save all experiment metadata, observations, and decisions in `results.json`, and save the visualization as `key_results.png`. Use `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`, `EXPERIMENT_SEED=20250308`, `TZ=UTC`, `LC_ALL=C.UTF-8`, and `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1704067200` in every measured execution. The package may use only bundled small data or deterministic data generated in code; measured containers must have networking disabled and must not install packages.
3. Before pulling, building, or creating any image, perform an early preflight. Verify that Docker or Podman responds within 10 seconds; the manifest's exact digest-pinned image is already present locally; its inspected architecture is `arm64`; it contains Python, `/usr/bin/strace`, and the package's required dependencies; the runtime can start a disposable container from it; the package and manifest are readable; and the filesystem holding the four run directories has at least 6 GiB free and at least 20,000 free inodes. Also verify that the package plus planned run directories will remain below any workspace quota, reserving at least 2 GiB of headroom. Never pull or build a fallback image inside the workspace.
