8. Start one new `--rm` container per execution from the exact locally present image digest. Mount the package read-only at `/package`, mount that run's empty output directory at the manifest-configured output location, make the container root filesystem read-only, provide fresh non-shared tmpfs mounts for `/tmp` and `/home/runner`, disable networking, set the fixed environment variables from step 2, set the working directory from the manifest, and share no caches, home directories, prior outputs, or writable volumes between runs. Do not use a long-lived container. Record the inspected image ID and digest for every run and require them to equal the manifest value.
