15. Use the strict decision rule: `supported` only if all four executions were completed from fresh containers, all four commands exited 0 without timeout, all 12 observations have `created_after_start=true`, all 12 have `write_before_read=true`, all 12 have `safety=true`, and all 12 have `digest_match=true`. If four valid executions and 12 parseable observations exist but any required boolean is false, or any command fails, classify the hypothesis as `refuted`. Use `inconclusive` only for preflight failure, parser-control failure, runtime infrastructure failure preventing four executions, or an incomplete/unparseable trace; never count an inconclusive case as support.
