Metrics to compute: Fresh execution completion count: number of distinct measured containers that reached termination and produced a complete parseable trace; required value is exactly 4., Target observation count: three manifest targets multiplied by four executions; required value is exactly 12., Creation rate: sum of `created_after_start=true` divided by 12, where creation requires pre-run absence and traced post-exec materialization; support threshold is 12/12 (100%)., Write-before-read rate: sum of `write_before_read=true` divided by 12 using positive-byte syscall events and file lineage; support threshold is 12/12 (100%)., Safety rate: sum of `safety=true` divided by 12 using containment, symlink, regular-file, hard-link, and lineage checks; support threshold is 12/12 (100%)., Digest reproduction rate: sum of exact assigned SHA-256 matches divided by 12; support threshold is 12/12 (100%)., Per-target reproducibility: for each of the three target paths, number of assigned-digest matches across four runs; each must equal 4/4., Complete-observation score: number of observations for which creation, write-before-read, safety, and digest match are all true; support threshold is 12/12., Parser-control accuracy: correctly classified expected outcomes divided by all synthetic and live control outcomes; required threshold before measured runs is 100%., Execution reliability: zero-exit, non-timeout runs divided by four; support threshold is 4/4.
